---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Security"
  description="ACQI security posture: where data lives, how access works, what is audited, and which certifications are planned rather than held."
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="micro micro--red mb-1 reveal">Trust</p>
      <h1 class="reveal reveal-2">Security stated as it is, including the gaps.</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal reveal-3">
        This page describes the product as it stands today. Where something is planned, it says
        planned. Where something is not done, it says so. A trust page that reads like a
        brochure is worse than no trust page at all.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">I</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Where the data lives</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cols cols--2">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            The product is installed inside the customer's environment. Estate data,
            credentials, evidence files and logs stay there. We do not operate a multi-tenant
            service, we do not receive a copy of your record, and there is no support tunnel into
            your installation that bypasses your access controls.
          </p>
          <p>
            The only outbound traffic the product initiates by default is the licence check. It
            carries a licence identifier and a version string. If you enable the optional error
            telemetry, it carries error signatures and counts, never entity names, file contents
            or credentials. Both can be disabled, and the licence check can be satisfied offline
            for air-gapped installations.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-0">
            This marketing website is a separate system. It is a static site hosted on Azure
            Static Web Apps. It sets no analytics cookies and loads no third-party scripts. See
            the <a href="/legal/privacy/">privacy notice</a> for what the contact form collects.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="micro mb-2">In the product</p>
          <dl class="defs" style="border-top:0">
            <div><dt>At rest</dt><dd>Database and evidence store encrypted with keys you hold.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>In transit</dt><dd>TLS 1.2 or later to every collector endpoint.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Credentials</dt><dd>Held in your secret store, brokered per run, never written to logs.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Audit</dt><dd>Every run, approval and export attributable to a named user.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Export</dt><dd>Documented schema, no proprietary format lock.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">II</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Access and permissions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cols cols--3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Read-only by default</h3>
          <p>Discovery credentials are scoped read-only. A discovery-only run will refuse a credential that carries write scope to a covered workload.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>No standing vendor access</h3>
          <p>We hold no persistent access to a customer installation. Support access is granted by you, time-boxed, and revoked by you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Least privilege inside the app</h3>
          <p>Roles separate discovery operators, reviewers and administrators. A reviewer can see a record without being able to re-run the collector that produced it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">III</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Compliance position</h2>
        <p class="micro section__note">Checked 17 November 2026</p>
      </div>

      <table class="table">
        <caption>Certifications and attestations</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Detail</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">ISO/IEC 27001</th>
            <td><span class="state state--planned">Planned</span></td>
            <td>Not held. A certification body has not been engaged. The target is certification after the entity is incorporated and the information security management system has run for a full audit cycle.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">SOC 2 Type II</th>
            <td><span class="state state--planned">Planned</span></td>
            <td>Not held. No observation period has started. Because the product is installed rather than hosted, the scope will cover the development and support organisation, not a service platform.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Cyber Essentials</th>
            <td><span class="state state--planned">Planned</span></td>
            <td>Not held. To be assessed after incorporation, since the scheme requires a legal entity.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">UK GDPR / DPA 2018</th>
            <td><span class="state">Designed for</span></td>
            <td>The installed model means we are not a processor of target data. Where we handle contact details through this site or a support relationship, the privacy notice sets out the basis and retention.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Penetration test</th>
            <td><span class="state state--none">Not yet</span></td>
            <td>No third-party test has been completed. One is scheduled before the first paid production licence. Results will be summarised here without the detail that would help an attacker.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Security questionnaire</th>
            <td><span class="state state--none">On request</span></td>
            <td>A current written response is available under NDA. It will include the unanswered items rather than omitting them.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="note mt-3">
        <p>
          <strong>If a procurement process requires a held certification, we will not pass it
          today.</strong> We would rather you know that before the questionnaire than after it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">IV</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Vulnerability handling and disclosure</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cols cols--2">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Dependencies are pinned and reviewed on a weekly cadence. Every release passes an
            automated dependency audit and a signed build. A severity-one issue in a shipped
            version triggers a security release, not a scheduled one.
          </p>
          <p>
            We accept reports from anyone. Send them to
            <a href={`mailto:${SITE.securityEmail}`}>{SITE.securityEmail}</a>, ideally with a
            reproduction. We will acknowledge within two working days, tell you what we intend
            to do, and credit you if you want credit.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-0">
            We will not pursue a researcher who acts in good faith, stays within the scope of
            their own installation or this website, and gives us a reasonable window before
            publishing. There is no paid bounty programme at this time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dl class="defs">
            <div><dt>Contact</dt><dd><a href={`mailto:${SITE.securityEmail}`}>{SITE.securityEmail}</a></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Machine readable</dt><dd><a href="/.well-known/security.txt">/.well-known/security.txt</a></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Acknowledgement</dt><dd>Two working days</dd></div>
            <div><dt>In scope</dt><dd>This website, shipped product builds, the installer and update channel</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Out of scope</dt><dd>Customer-operated infrastructure, third-party cloud services, social engineering</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">V</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Subprocessors</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cols cols--sidebar">
        <p class="lede mb-0">For the product: none. For this website: one.</p>
        <div>
          <p>
            <strong>Microsoft Azure Static Web Apps</strong> hosts this site and runs the two
            functions behind the contact form and the preview gate. It processes request logs and
            the contents of a contact submission. Region: West US 2. No other processor receives
            data from this site.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-0">
            The product itself has no subprocessors, because it runs in your environment. If that
            ever changes, this page changes first.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
